          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people, the best backup battery supply for a computer is the CyberPower CP1500PFCLCD: 1,000W of pure sine wave output, voltage regulation and enough runtime to save your work and shut down cleanly, for well under the price of business-grade units. APC loyalists should buy the Back-UPS Pro BR1500MS2, office PCs can step down to the CP1000PFCLCD, and a modem and router need nothing more than the APC BE600M1.
